=== DESIGN ===
intervals.go: categoryDefaults table + fieldOverrides table + IntervalFor(field) (int,bool).
  setting_unit=1, driving/location/powertrain=5, charging=10, climate/safety_security/vehicle_state=30, media/config/prefs/metadata=60.
  overrides: VehicleSpeed=1, Gear=1, BatteryLevel=30 (each commented w/ reason).
config.go: Builder{Hostname,Port}, NewBuilder, SubscriptionFields(), BuildSubscription(), BuildFor(vins).
  iterates protomodel.Signals once, skips Category=='metadata', sorts alphabetically, fills templates/full_subscription.json.tmpl, validates+pretty-prints via encoding/json round-trip for byte-stable output.
  no HTTP — delivery owned by client_fleet_telemetry.go per ADR-004.
=== UNIT_TEST ===
TestConfigCoversAllFields: enumerates protomodel.Signals reflectively, asserts every non-metadata Field appears with positive interval_seconds, asserts every IsSettingUnit field has interval_seconds==1 — fails loudly with the missing field name.
TestSubscriptionDeterministic: builds twice + asserts byte-equality + asserts BuildFor is order-independent on VIN list.
TestBuildForIncludesVINs: round-trips hostname/port/VINs through the rendered body.
TestIntervalForKnownAndUnknownFields: exercises override path + setting_unit category + unknown-field guard returning ok=false.
